// T1 — Your workspace gets Sift, and its history becomes the first pass
// Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md ("S:n" = its line n) and the accepted ADRs docs/adrs/SIFT-ADR-0*.md.
// Founder ruling 2026-11-04: Source = "Spec of record". NDD-SOURCE.md is a derived document: it gives the thread structure and the titles only; where it differs from the spec, the spec wins.
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T1.O1 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
//   T1.M1 · An operator turns Sift on: CreateACustomerWorkspaceWithEnable (former flow t1-create-a-customer-workspace-with-enable.moment)
//   T1.M1 · An operator turns Sift on (continued): EnableOnAnEnabledWorkspaceReturnsTheLatestSiftEnabled (former flow t1-enable-on-an-enabled-workspace-returns-the-latest-siftenabled.moment)
//   T1.M2 · Sift is made ready to hold your design: ASetupStepFails (former flow t1-a-setup-step-fails.moment)
//   T1.M2 · Sift is made ready to hold your design: TheWorkspaceIsReadyThroughAnotherSiftEnabled (former flow t1-the-workspace-is-ready-through-another-siftenabled.moment)
//   T1.M3 · Your history is read, in order (continued): AChildCyclesEntryFailsAndTheReplayGoesOn (former flow t1-a-child-cycles-entry-fails-and-the-replay-goes-on.moment)
//   T1.M3 · Your history is read, in order (continued): TheHistoryHoldsAnErasureStreamEntry (former flow t1-the-history-holds-an-erasure-stream-entry.moment)
// REFUSALS BY A PRECONDITION on a command of the main path (derived as negative scenarios for every path of the flow, Moment 0.9.0 ADR-042) (a derived `neg-<Command>-<Precondition>` scenario; no branch moment, because the spec names no
// next step for the valid arm of a guard that is one of the command's own refusals): T1.M1·B1 EnableSift.NotOperator; T1.M1·B2 EnableSift.EntitlementActive and
// EnableSift.FlmntWorkspaceExists (T1.N1); T1.M1·B3 EnableSift.NoOpAlreadyEnabled; T1.M2·B1 ProvisionAgentWorkspace.CreateIfAbsent and StartKeyGeneration.NoOpNotNext;
// T1.M4·B1 CompleteSetup.KeyGenerationCurrent and CompleteSetup.NoOpAlreadyCompleted.
// DIFFERENCES FROM NDD-SOURCE (the spec wins): the Sift-workspaces read model (NDD "RM5") is drawn once, at the terminal, where the spec folds it from SiftEnabled (S:1421) and
// "ready" is stated (S:238); the Replay's `FEED`/`QANS` crossings are not in the spec (it says only "flmnt -> C2 ... the feed, request and erasure streams", S:185).
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T1 — Your workspace gets Sift, and its history becomes the first pass"
  description "T1 — Your workspace gets Sift, and its history becomes the first pass. The story of the thread from its start to its T1.O1 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane enablement "Enablement" [Supporting]
  lane intake "Intake" [Core]
  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]
  lane clarification "Clarification" [Core]

  moment "T1.M1 · An operator turns Sift on" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // [person] an operator (owner, admin or architect on the customer workspace) asks to enable Sift  // S:219 "requires an operator claim on the customer workspace"
      // [management API] EnableSift(Person) on one customer workspace, exempt from the gate, idempotent by the caller's request key  // S:281 "EnableSift(Person) on one customer workspace (operator on it), exempt from the gate"
      // The License-scope EnableSift(Person) fans out one request per customer workspace, each checking the operator claim on its own workspace (a fan-out, not declarable)  // S:288 "which fans out one request per customer workspace"
      enablement: EnableSift cause Person  // S:203 "EnableSift(origin: Person | Reactivation | Reconciliation, entitlement, billingEventId?)"
    when CreateACustomerWorkspaceWithEnable
      // former flow: t1-create-a-customer-workspace-with-enable.moment
      // T1.M1 · An operator turns Sift on
      // [person] an operator on the license creates a customer workspace with enable  // S:287 "CreateCustomerWorkspace{enable?} (operator on the license, checked before the gateway is called; its Cycle calls the gateway, keyed by the request key of the request"
      // the chained enable's own Cycle reads the owner claim from the recorded gateway result of the creation  // S:219 "that claim is the creator's owner role: the gateway call is made on behalf of the caller"
      enablement: CreateCustomerWorkspace  // S:287 "CreateCustomerWorkspace{enable?} (operator on the license, checked before the gateway is called; its Cycle calls the gateway, keyed by the request key of the request"
      design: RecordGatewayResult  // S:966 "RecordGatewayResult(license, customer workspace, owner sub, request key, enable flag, creator);"
      design: GatewayResultRecorded  // S:978 "GatewayResultRecorded {license, customer workspace, owner sub, request key, enable flag, creator}"
      design: RecordNodeChange  // S:903 "RecordNodeChange(write Pointer or RecordRef, CycleId) (NEW) records NodeChanged"
      design: NodeChanged  // S:979 "ReplayCompleted, ReadModelsDestroyed, DocumentVersionProcessed, PassTriggerRecorded and GatewayResultRecorded are writes for which RecordNodeChange records NodeChanged"
      // a new unit of work of its own, in its own Cycle after the creation, exempt from the gate (S:288)
      enablement: EnableSift cause Person  // S:288 "a policy on the GatewayResultRecorded of the creation issues the per-workspace EnableSift(Person) request as a new unit of work"
        triggered-by GatewayResultRecorded  // S:288 "a policy on the GatewayResultRecorded of the creation issues the per-workspace EnableSift(Person) request as a new unit of work" (policy ChainedEnableOnGatewayResult)
      enablement: SiftEnabled [outcome]  // S:210 "SiftEnabled {origin, personallyEnabled, billingEventId?}"

  moment "T1.M1 · An operator turns Sift on (continued)" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      enablement: SiftEnabled  // S:210 "SiftEnabled {origin, personallyEnabled, billingEventId?}"
    when EnableOnAnEnabledWorkspaceReturnsTheLatestSiftEnabled
      // former flow: t1-enable-on-an-enabled-workspace-returns-the-latest-siftenabled.moment
      // Outcome: the workspace is already enabled (Round 6 D-3), so nothing new is recorded. The same case is the precondition EnableSift.NoOpAlreadyEnabled.
      // T1.M1·B3 · when the workspace is already enabled (D-3)
      // when the latest lifecycle event is a SiftEnabled: nothing new is recorded; its unit of work then runs the setup from the current state, a no-op when the workspace is ready  // S:220 "Its unit of work then runs the setup from the current state for that SiftEnabled, which on a ready workspace runs step 4"
      enablement: SiftEnabled [outcome]  // S:220 "it records nothing new and returns that SiftEnabled"

  moment "T1.M2 · Sift is made ready to hold your design" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // Setup runs inside the unit of work that records SiftEnabled e; each step reads SiftEnablement's recorded events when it runs  // S:242 "Each step reads SiftEnablement's recorded events when it runs."
      // [flmnt] the agent-workspace link, create-if-absent, external key hash(customer workspace)  // S:224 "ProvisionAgentWorkspace is create-if-absent (external key hash(customer workspace))"
      enablement: ProvisionAgentWorkspace  // S:243 "**Provision**, if not provisioned."
        triggered-by SiftEnabled  // S:243 "1. Provision, if not provisioned." (policy SetupStep1Provision)
      enablement: AgentWorkspaceProvisioned  // S:212 "AgentWorkspaceProvisioned {WorkspaceLink}"
      // No earlier key generation, so no rebuild  // S:246 "if the current key generation n follows a retired one"
      enablement: StartKeyGeneration  // S:245 "StartKeyGeneration(current + 1)"
      enablement: KeyGenerationStarted  // S:213 "KeyGenerationStarted {n}"
    when ASetupStepFails
      // former flow: t1-a-setup-step-fails.moment
      // Outcome: a setup step (provision, key generation, the Replay as a whole, CompleteSetup or the setup pass) fails after brief retries; the setup ends Failed with an alarm, the workspace is enabled but not ready, and gated work is Postponed.
      // T1.M4·B3 · when a setup step fails (provision, key generation, the Replay as a whole, CompleteSetup or the setup pass)
      // when a setup step fails: the setup ends Failed with an alarm; it is redone by the next tick (D-4), an operator's RedriveCycle or a person's new enable request; a setup always works from the current lifecycle state  // S:260 "a setup that fails after brief retries ends Failed with an alarm"
      design: RecordStepFailure  // S:1407 "RecordStepFailure | the Cycle's executor, when a step fails after its brief retries"
      design: SagaStepFailed  // S:926 "RecordStepFailure (NEW), issued by the executor when a step fails after its brief retries, records SagaStepFailed before CompleteCycle records CycleCompleted{Failed}"
      design: CompleteCycle  // S:905 "CompleteCycle(outcome, failedCommands?, ingressEffect?, constructStates, designState, position) (NEW), issued by the Cycle's executor when the unit of work ends"
      design: CycleCompleted [terminal]  // S:905 "CycleCompleted {outcome: Succeeded | Failed"
    when TheWorkspaceIsReadyThroughAnotherSiftEnabled
      // former flow: t1-the-workspace-is-ready-through-another-siftenabled.moment
      // Outcome: the workspace is ready through another SiftEnabled f with no SetupCompleted for e, so step 3 and CompleteSetup are skipped and only f's pass, if it is missing, runs.
      // T1.M4·B2 · when the setup is ready through another SiftEnabled f with no SetupCompleted for e
      // when ready through another SiftEnabled f with no SetupCompleted for e: step 3 and CompleteSetup are skipped; only f's pass, if it is missing, runs  // S:257 "step 3 and CompleteSetup are skipped (run-1 B13). Only f's pass, if it is missing, runs."
      design: StartPass  // S:255 "the customer workspace is ready through another SiftEnabled's SetupCompleted f → StartPass in the same Cycle"
      design: PassStarted  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      design: RecordGateResults  // S:669 "RecordGateResults(sequence number, evaluated constructs[], findings[])"
        triggered-by PassStarted  // S:720 "Gate run: PassStarted → GateRun" (policy PassStartedRunsGates)
      design: GatesEvaluated  // S:674 "GatesEvaluated {judgements}"
      design: CompletePass  // S:723 "**Completion:** GatesEvaluated → CompletePass."
        triggered-by GatesEvaluated  // S:723 "Completion: GatesEvaluated → CompletePass" (policy GatesEvaluatedCompletesPass)
      design: PassCompleted [outcome]  // S:675 "PassCompleted {ConvergenceSnapshot, verdict, actor, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion, startPosition, asOf, CauseKey}"

  moment "T1.M3 · Your history is read, in order"
    // Setup step 3, kind Bootstrap (not bootstrapped), from the stream start; end point = per stream, the stream head read when e is taken  // S:251 "kind = **Bootstrap** if not bootstrapped (from the stream start)"
    // Replay step 1: in order and one at a time; each other entry runs as a child Cycle with RecordReceipt and Arrival Replay(Bootstrap)  // S:385 "Each other entry runs as a child Cycle, with RecordReceipt and Dispatch of Entry dispatch, and Arrival Replay(Bootstrap | Resume)"
    // The parent applies the cheap checks; a filtered entry starts no Cycle  // S:385 "The parent applies the cheap checks, and a filtered entry starts no Cycle"
    // Extraction and Placement of each entry are T3; a replayed boundary entry runs the question sweep and posts nothing (T2.M6); no model-wide pass starts  // S:359 "**Nothing model-wide starts inside a Replay or an intake.**"
    intake: RecordReceipt  // S:369 "**RecordReceipt(Pointer, Arrival).**"
    intake: ReceiptRecorded  // S:321 "ReceiptRecorded {Arrival};"

  moment "T1.M3 · Your history is read, in order (continued)" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // Replay step 2, Complete: record ReplayCompleted {Bootstrap}; the setup then records SetupCompleted and runs the pass (S:386)
      design: CompleteReplay  // S:962 "CompleteReplay(kind, SiftEnabled: EventRef, replay point and end point per stream);"
      design: ReplayCompleted  // S:386 "CompleteReplay(kind, SiftEnabled: EventRef, replay point and end point per stream) (NEW) records ReplayCompleted {Bootstrap | Resume, replay point and end point per stream}"
      design: RecordNodeChange  // S:903 "RecordNodeChange(write Pointer or RecordRef, CycleId) (NEW) records NodeChanged"
      design: NodeChanged  // S:979 "ReplayCompleted, ReadModelsDestroyed, DocumentVersionProcessed, PassTriggerRecorded and GatewayResultRecorded are writes for which RecordNodeChange records NodeChanged"
    when AChildCyclesEntryFailsAndTheReplayGoesOn
      // former flow: t1-a-child-cycles-entry-fails-and-the-replay-goes-on.moment
      // Outcome: a child Cycle's entry fails; it is a failed attempt, redone by the next live arrival and quarantined at the bound, and the Replay is not stopped (failure thread T9).
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T1.M4 · Setup is recorded and the first pass runs: enablement: SetupCompleted [terminal]  // S:215 "SetupCompleted {kind, SiftEnabled: EventRef, keyGeneration}"
      // T1.M3·B1 · when a child Cycle's entry fails
      // when a child Cycle's entry fails: the Replay goes on; the entry follows the entry-failure rule (redone by the next live arrival, quarantined at the bound)  // S:385 "A child Cycle whose entry fails doesn't stop the Replay"
      intake: RecordFailedAttempt  // S:345 "RecordFailedAttempt(cycleId, Pointer, Arrival)** is issued when an entry's processing fails"
      intake: AttemptFailed  // S:323 "AttemptFailed {cycleId, attempt, quarantined};"
      // T1.M3 · The Replay completes
      design: CompleteReplay  // S:962 "CompleteReplay(kind, SiftEnabled: EventRef, replay point and end point per stream);"
      design: ReplayCompleted  // S:386 "CompleteReplay(kind, SiftEnabled: EventRef, replay point and end point per stream) (NEW) records ReplayCompleted {Bootstrap | Resume, replay point and end point per stream}"
      design: RecordNodeChange  // S:903 "RecordNodeChange(write Pointer or RecordRef, CycleId) (NEW) records NodeChanged"
      design: NodeChanged  // S:979 "ReplayCompleted, ReadModelsDestroyed, DocumentVersionProcessed, PassTriggerRecorded and GatewayResultRecorded are writes for which RecordNodeChange records NodeChanged"
    when TheHistoryHoldsAnErasureStreamEntry
      // former flow: t1-the-history-holds-an-erasure-stream-entry.moment
      // Outcome: an entry of the erasure stream is dispatched in order as ReadModelDestruction (the Replay goes on; erasure thread T7).
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T1.M3 · Your history is read, in order: Replay step 1 dispatches the erasure stream too, in order, one at a time  // S:385 "The Replay reads each consumed stream (feed history with causal links, request stream, erasure stream)"
      // T1.M3·B2 · when the history holds an erasure-stream entry
      // when the history holds an erasure-stream entry: ReadModelDestruction (entry scope) dispatched in order; the Replay goes on (NDD: returns-to T1.M3); erasure thread T7  // S:373 "erasure stream: ReadModelDestruction(entry scope)"
      design: ReadModelDestruction [outcome]  // S:373 "erasure stream: ReadModelDestruction(entry scope)"

  moment "T1.M4 · Setup is recorded and the first pass runs"
    // Setup step 4, complete then pass: CompleteSetup, then StartPass in the same Cycle with the kind and the derived pass ID of that SetupCompleted  // S:254 "CompleteSetup(kind, e, n)"
    enablement: CompleteSetup  // S:208 "CompleteSetup(kind: Bootstrap | Resume, SiftEnabled: EventRef, keyGeneration)"
      triggered-by ReplayCompleted  // S:254 "If no SetupCompleted for e exists and the customer workspace is not ready → CompleteSetup(kind, e, n)." (policy SetupStep4Complete)
    enablement: SetupCompleted  // S:256 "SetupCompleted is recorded before the pass, so it doesn't wait for it"
    // The setup pass is the Replay's own end pass and declares the verdict  // S:385 "the Bootstrap or Resume pass of the setup is the Replay's own end pass and declares the verdict"
    design: StartPass  // S:255 "StartPass in the same Cycle, with the kind and the derived pass ID of that SetupCompleted"
      triggered-by SetupCompleted  // S:255 "If a SetupCompleted for e exists, or the customer workspace is ready through another SiftEnabled's SetupCompleted f → StartPass in the same Cycle" (policy SetupStep4StartsPass)
    design: PassStarted  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
    // PassStarted -> GateRun (domain service): catch-up, evaluate the rules of the effective catalogue (C5: RulesVersion read at startPosition); a finding is GapIdentified -> ObserveGap (T3.M5, T4.M1)  // S:720 "**Gate run:** PassStarted → **GateRun**"
    design: RecordGateResults  // S:669 "RecordGateResults(sequence number, evaluated constructs[], findings[])"
      triggered-by PassStarted  // S:720 "Gate run: PassStarted → GateRun" (policy PassStartedRunsGates)
    design: GatesEvaluated  // S:674 "GatesEvaluated {judgements}"
    design: CompletePass  // S:723 "**Completion:** GatesEvaluated → CompletePass."
      triggered-by GatesEvaluated  // S:723 "Completion: GatesEvaluated → CompletePass" (policy GatesEvaluatedCompletesPass)
    design: PassCompleted  // S:675 "PassCompleted {ConvergenceSnapshot, verdict, actor, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion, startPosition, asOf, CauseKey}"
    design: ConstructCleared  // S:723 "records PassCompleted plus ConstructCleared for each evaluated construct with no blocking Gap"
    design: CommitConstruct  // S:724 "ConstructCleared → CommitConstruct."
      triggered-by ConstructCleared  // S:724 "ConstructCleared → CommitConstruct" (policy ConstructClearedCommits)
    design: ConstructCommitted  // S:554 "ConstructCommitted;"

  moment "T1.M5 · The questions of your history arrive once, together"
    // [flmnt] posting is a side effect of the question poster, an external call with a key, not a command (`QPOST`, one post per base subject)  // S:1085 "are side effects of the question and notice poster, an external call with a key, not commands"
    // The Replay's one flush follows the setup pass: the gathered postings are flushed once, as at a session boundary  // S:258 "**The Replay's one flush follows the pass**"
    // QuestionCompounded (an open generation) and QuestionReaddressed (the step-2 rebuild or a tick) are not on this spine (T4.M2, T8)  // S:1027 "On an open generation it records QuestionCompounded."
    clarification: AskQuestion  // S:1027 "AskQuestion(causedBy, recipientRule)"
    clarification: QuestionAsked [terminal]  // S:1086 "QuestionAsked, QuestionCompounded and QuestionReaddressed → **gathered** until the customer workspace's next session boundary"

  moment "T1.O1 · Sift is ready (terminal)"
    // PROVES: SiftEnabled, AgentWorkspaceProvisioned, KeyGenerationStarted, ReplayCompleted, SetupCompleted and a PassCompleted are recorded; ready is stated at S:238  // S:238 "**ready** = provisioned ∧ the current key generation is not retired ∧ a SetupCompleted exists **whose SiftEnabled ref comes after the latest SiftDisabled**"
    note enablement: "The Sift-workspaces read model folds SiftEnabled and SiftDisabled"  // S:1421 "Sift-workspaces (the customer workspaces that have Sift) | SiftEnabled · SiftDisabled"
